00:40:47.520 --> 00:40:48.670
<v Wbez Operator>[DIALING]
<v Wbez Operator>[拨号]

00:40:48.670 --> 00:41:22.460
<v Michael Stumm>Hi, Ira, this is Michael in South Africa. Listen, about the item that we spoke about, the turkey's head attached to the turkey's foot, well, I spoke to some sangomas, which are witch doctors in the neighborhood about that thing. And they've never heard of anything quite like it or seen anything quite like it. However, when I would describe it to them, their jaws dropped. But look, I discovered a whole bunch about poultry in South Africa, so call me back, OK?
<v Michael Stumm>嗨，艾拉，我是南非的迈克尔。听着，关于我们谈到的那件东西，那个连着脚的火鸡头，我问了一些桑格玛，就是我们这儿的巫医，关于那个东西。他们以前从未听说过或见过类似的东西。然而，当我向他们描述它时，他们惊得下巴都掉了。但听着，我在南非发现了很多关于家禽的事情，所以给我回电话，好吗？

00:41:22.460 --> 00:41:51.110
<v Ira Glass>Well, Michael is Michael Stumm, performer, actor, former member of The Wooster Group in New York City. A former Chicagoan, now lives in Johannesburg, South Africa. And I asked him to look into the uses of chicken and other poultry among the sangoma culture in South Africa. Sangomas, or witch doctors or herbalists or orators, you hear them called sometimes, they're common in South Africa. Everybody seems to know one. And chickens are one of their main tools.
<v Ira Glass>迈克尔是迈克尔·斯图姆，表演者、演员，纽约伍斯特剧团的前成员。曾住芝加哥，现住南非约翰内斯堡。我请他调查一下南非桑格玛文化中对鸡和其他禽类的使用情况。桑格玛，或称巫医、草药师或演说家，有时你会听到这么叫，在南非很普遍。每个人似乎都认识一个。鸡是他们主要工具之一。

00:41:51.110 --> 00:42:36.400
<v Michael Stumm>Well, it's a funny thing. I've discovered that over half the country is just awash in chicken blood. It's a substance that comes in so handy. It's rather like-- gosh, I don't know-- it flows like milk does in America or Dr. Bronner's chamomile soap or some other easily spilled liquid in modern America. It's an incredibly versatile product. You can lose bad luck with it. You can strengthen a faulty muscle with it. You can improve your eyesight with it. You can find lost items with it. You can get your wife back with it. You can transfer your bad luck to someone else with it.
<v Michael Stumm>嗯，这很有趣。我发现这个国家的一半地区到处都是鸡血。这是一种很方便的物质。它有点像——天哪，我不知道——它像美国的牛奶、布朗纳博士的甘菊皂，或者现代美国其他容易洒出的液体那样流动。这是一种令人难以置信的多功能产品。你可以用它消除厄运。你可以用它强健虚弱的肌肉。你可以用它改善视力。你可以用它找回丢失的物品。你可以用它挽回妻子的心。你可以用它把厄运转移到别人身上。

00:42:36.400 --> 00:42:51.340
<v Michael Stumm>I mean, I had someone tell me that there is a ceremony involving the killing of a chicken in a rather baroque manner, which I'll describe to you. But this is a very specific ceremony that involved losing your court papers at court.
<v Michael Stumm>我是说，有人告诉我有一种仪式涉及以一种相当华丽的方式杀鸡，我会为你描述的。但这是一种非常具体的仪式，涉及让你在法庭上丢失你的诉讼文件。

00:42:51.340 --> 00:42:57.580
<v Ira Glass>In other words, if you do this thing with this chicken, the court will lose the papers, and that's how you will go free?
<v Ira Glass>换句话说，如果你对这只鸡做了这件事，法院就会丢失文件，你就可以因此无罪释放？

00:42:57.580 --> 00:42:59.730
<v Michael Stumm>Allow me to describe the ceremony.
<v Michael Stumm>请允许我描述这个仪式。

00:42:59.730 --> 00:43:08.720
<v Ira Glass>Sure, because I'm sure many of our listeners get into these kinds of situations and have wondered, how can we make, for example, the US District Attorney simply lose that file?
<v Ira Glass>当然，因为我相信许多听众都会陷入这种境地，并想知道，我们如何能让美国联邦检察官直接丢失那个档案？

00:43:08.720 --> 00:43:56.930
<v Michael Stumm>Yeah, you are arrested. A court date is set. You then go home to your witch doctor. You bring him a white chicken. It has to be a white chicken. The witch doctor then prescribes some muti, which is medicine. It can come in many, many forms. Perhaps it's a powder. Perhaps it's a liquid. It doesn't really matter because you're going to take the muti yourself. You then take the chicken and the muti to the nearest mountain. You climb to the top of the mountain. You dig a hole. You dig a hole large enough for the chicken to fit in. You then speak to the chicken. You say to the chicken, "This is what I want to have happen. I would like my United States federal court tax document, file number 869102b, to disappear." Or whatever it is that you want to disappear.
<v Michael Stumm>是的，你被逮捕了。法庭日期定下来了。然后你回家找你的巫医。你带给他一只白鸡。必须是白鸡。巫医然后开出一些“穆蒂”，就是药。它可以有很多很多种形式。也许是粉末，也许是液体。这没关系，因为你自己要服用那个穆蒂。然后你带着鸡和穆蒂去最近的山。你爬到山顶。你挖一个洞。挖一个足够装下那只鸡的洞。然后你对鸡说话。你对鸡说：“这就是我想要发生的。我想要我的美国联邦法院税务文件，档案号869102b，消失。”或者任何你想要消失的东西。

00:43:56.930 --> 00:44:09.810
<v Michael Stumm>You then take a large sewing needle, and you poke the chicken's eyes out with this sewing needle. You then bury the chicken, the now blind chicken, alive in the hole. You put him in the hole. You put the dirt back on.
<v Michael Stumm>然后你拿一根大缝衣针，用这根针把鸡的眼睛戳瞎。然后你把那只鸡，那只现在眼瞎的鸡，活着埋进洞里。把它放进洞里。把土盖回去。

00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:21.800
<v Ira Glass>Then this chicken is going to do something for you in the afterworld after you've poked out its eyes and you're burying it alive? This chicken is going to do you a favor among the mystic spirits?
<v Ira Glass>那这只鸡在你戳瞎它的眼睛并把它活埋之后，会在来世为你做什么？这只鸡会在神秘灵魂之间为你提供帮助吗？

00:44:21.800 --> 00:44:40.300
<v Michael Stumm>Magic is funny, Ira. What can I say? Essentially, it's the end of the ceremony. You leave the chicken, and then you go. And as it was described to me, you go back to your court date on the day of your court date, and your papers will be lost. People will say to you, "You have no papers. You are free." That's how it was described to me.
<v Michael Stumm>魔法很有趣，艾拉。我能说什么呢？基本上，仪式到此结束。你把鸡留在那里，然后就走了。正如人们对我描述的那样，你在开庭之日回到法庭，你的文件就会丢失。人们会告诉你：“你没有任何文件。你是自由的。”这就是人们向我描述的情况。

00:44:40.300 --> 00:44:51.030
<v Ira Glass>Now, Mr. Stumm, in the interest of accurate reporting, have you talked to anyone who claims that this worked for them personally?
<v Ira Glass>那么，斯图姆先生，出于准确报道的考虑，你有没有和任何人谈过，他们声称这真的对他们个人有效？

00:44:51.030 --> 00:45:19.870
<v Michael Stumm>Well, the gentleman I spoke to has heard of this working. He has not actually been arrested himself and caused his papers to disappear in this manner. But apparently, there are gangs of chicken rustlers here, not unlike cattle rustling in Western movies.
<v Michael Stumm>嗯，我谈过的那位先生听说过这真的有效。他本人并没有被逮捕过，也没有用这种方式让自己的文件消失。但显然，这里有成群的“鸡窃贼”，就像西部片里的偷牛贼一样。

00:45:19.870 --> 00:45:20.480
<v Ira Glass>You're making this up.
<v Ira Glass>你在胡扯。

00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:21.400
<v Michael Stumm>Cattle rustlers.
<v Michael Stumm>偷牛贼。

00:45:21.400 --> 00:45:23.200
<v Ira Glass>Chicken rustlers.
<v Ira Glass>鸡窃贼。

00:45:23.200 --> 00:45:25.030
<v Michael Stumm>Chicken rustlers, I swear.
<v Michael Stumm>鸡窃贼，我发誓。

00:45:25.030 --> 00:45:29.900
<v Ira Glass>What kind of dignity is there in that for a man? Let me just ask you that.
<v Ira Glass>作为一个男人，那有什么尊严可言？我只想问你。

00:45:29.900 --> 00:45:31.150
<v Michael Stumm>Chicken rustling?
<v Michael Stumm>偷鸡？

00:45:31.150 --> 00:46:05.280
<v Ira Glass>Yeah, you rustle some cattle, and you feel like a man. But you rustle a chicken, I mean, the word rustle doesn't even seem like it's the right word. It's just too big a word. It's too grand a word. You don't hear the strands of Aaron Copland when the word rustle comes up next to the word chicken. Hold on for a second. I'm just going to put on some Aaron Copland here right now. I just wanted you to conjure a scene of the chicken rustlers. Could you just describe how you picture them? The music is going now.
<v Ira Glass>是啊，你偷牛，感觉像个男人。但你偷鸡，我是说，连“偷”这个词听起来都不太对。这个词太大了。太宏大了。当你把偷这个词和鸡连在一起时，你听不到阿隆·科普兰音乐的旋律。等等，我现在就要放点阿隆·科普兰的音乐。我只是想让你想象一下偷鸡贼的场景。你能描述一下你眼中的他们吗？音乐正在播放。

00:46:05.280 --> 00:46:43.480
<v Michael Stumm>Well, I think as I picture a chicken rustle, they probably wait until the sun goes down. And they probably have a sack, because if you stick a chicken in a sack, she is not going to make noise. So they probably chuck a bunch of chickens in the sack, as many as they can get away with until the chickens who are not in the sack start making noise. And then they run away. That's how I envision a chicken rustling.
<v Michael Stumm>嗯，我想在我想象中的偷鸡过程中，他们大概会等到天黑。他们大概会有一个麻袋，因为如果你把鸡塞进麻袋里，它就不会发出噪音。所以他们大概会把一大堆鸡塞进麻袋里，能拿多少就拿多少，直到还没进麻袋的鸡开始发出噪音。然后他们就跑了。这就是我设想的偷鸡场景。

00:46:43.480 --> 00:46:55.760
<v Ira Glass>Michael, do chicken rustlers ever get rustled themselves? I mean is it like the mafia, where it goes back and forth and back and forth in an endless cycle of violence and rustling?
<v Ira Glass>迈克尔，鸡窃贼会被别人偷吗？我是说，这就像黑手党，暴力和偷窃没完没了的循环吗？

00:46:55.760 --> 00:48:30.890
<v Michael Stumm>Luca Brasi sleeps with the chickens. I don't know.
<v Michael Stumm>卢卡·布拉西和鸡一起睡。我不知道。

00:48:30.890 --> 00:49:17.360
<v Ira Glass>Act Five, Chickenman, Like the Phoenix. As a child, I did not care about the radio. In fact, I have to say that there was only one thing that I remember hearing on the radio up until the age of 16, I'd say. And that was Chickenman. It had all these qualities of radio that I've since come to value. It was surprising. It was funny. It had its own sound, a sound that was completely distinctive and instantly recognizable and appealing. Dick Orkin was the voice of Chickenman, and in the years since Chickenman, he's done tons of work, including lots of commercials in that deadpan style, a style which hundreds of people all over the country have tried to imitate. Nobody ever gets it right.
<v Ira Glass>第五幕，鸡侠，如凤凰涅槃。小时候，我不关心广播。事实上，不得不说，在我16岁之前，我记得在收音机里听到的东西只有一样，那就是鸡侠。它具备了我后来所珍视的所有广播品质。它出人意料。它很有趣。它有自己的声音，一种完全独特、瞬间可辨且迷人的声音。迪克·奥金是鸡侠的配音，在鸡侠之后的岁月里，他做了大量工作，包括许多那种冷面幽默风格的广告，全国成百上千人试图模仿这种风格。从来没有人模仿得对。

00:49:17.360 --> 00:49:43.590
<v Ira Glass>And it's a pleasure, it's an honor to have him on our program. Last year when This American Life was just a local program in Chicago, before you could hear it around the country, we invited Dick Orkin to create a new Chickenman episode for our Poultry Slam. And he put a cast together, put together the first new episode since 1969. In this episode, Chickenman is a quarter century older, like his creator, and he faces a new set of problems.
<v Ira Glass>很高兴、很荣幸能请他上我们的节目。去年当《美国生活》还只是芝加哥当地的一档节目，在你能在全国范围内听到它之前，我们邀请迪克·奥金为我们的“家禽大满贯”创作了一部新的鸡侠剧集。他召集了一个演员阵容，完成了1969年以来的第一部新剧集。在这一集中，鸡侠和他的创作者一样，老了四分之一个世纪，他面临着一系列新的问题。

00:49:43.590 --> 00:49:56.020
<v Chickenman Announcer>Now, another exciting episode in the life of the most fantastic crime fighter the world has ever known, Chickenman.
<v Chickenman Announcer>现在，世界上最了不起的犯罪克星——鸡侠生命中又一段激动人心的插曲。

00:49:56.020 --> 00:50:00.380
<v Women>He's everywhere! He's everywhere!
<v Women>他无处不在！他无处不在！

00:50:00.380 --> 00:50:21.200
<v Chickenman>Tuesday morning, 9:30 AM. The chicken alarm in my chicken cave goes off 30 minutes late, which makes me late for my annual physical at my doctor, [? Dupont ?] Chopper. I didn't want to be late since it was my first in 30 years. 9:50 AM. I get a flat as I pull the chicken Coupe out of the chicken garage. So I take the convenient number 32 bus, which drops me off only 14 blocks from the doctor's office.
<v Chickenman>周二早上，9:30。我鸡窟里的鸡报警器晚了30分钟才响，这让我去医生那里的年度体检迟到了。我不想迟到，因为这是我30年来的第一次体检。9:50。我把鸡轿车开出鸡库时爆胎了。所以我坐了方便的32路公交车，它把我放在离医生办公室只有14个街区的地方。

00:50:21.200 --> 00:50:23.530
<v Doctor>You're late. You're late for a very important date.
<v Doctor>你迟到了。你迟到了，错过了一个非常重要的约会。

00:50:23.530 --> 00:50:27.450
<v Chickenman>Says the doctor, and I say, "I know. I'm sorry. All the air went out of my whatchamacallit."
<v Chickenman>医生说，我说：“我知道。对不起。我的那个什么什么东西全没气了。”

00:50:27.450 --> 00:50:32.260
<v Doctor>That happens to all of us. Age. Try not to sit on sharp things, and don't think sharp things.
<v Doctor>这种情况我们都有。年纪大了。尽量不要坐在尖锐的东西上，也不要思考尖锐的东西。

00:50:32.260 --> 00:50:32.690
<v Chickenman>OK.
<v Chickenman>好的。

00:50:32.690 --> 00:50:36.770
<v Doctor>Body, mind, mind body in all you do. And Santa Claus is watching you.
<v Doctor>身体，头脑，头脑带动身体，做你所做的一切。圣诞老人正在看着你。

00:50:36.770 --> 00:50:39.910
<v Chickenman>11:00 AM, after several tests and poking and prodding.
<v Chickenman>11:00 AM，经过几次测试和戳戳点点后。

00:50:39.910 --> 00:50:45.300
<v Doctor>Well, your cholesterol is a little high. The pain in your toes is arthritis, and I think you have the beginning of a nice hernia.
<v Doctor>嗯，你的胆固醇有点高。脚趾的疼痛是关节炎，我想你开始长了一个漂亮的疝气。

00:50:45.300 --> 00:50:47.880
<v Chickenman>Cholesterol high, I had no idea.
<v Chickenman>胆固醇高，我完全不知道。

00:50:47.880 --> 00:51:00.190
<v Doctor>Well, technically it's not high because one, it is in your mind. And two, it is your bad cholesterol that's bad. Your good cholesterol is not good, but in time, your cholesterol will be good, and your good cholesterol will be bad. And that's not good.
<v Doctor>嗯，严格来说它不高，因为第一，它在你的脑子里。第二，这是你的坏胆固醇，确实不好。你的好胆固醇也不好，但久而久之，你的胆固醇会变好，你的好胆固醇会变坏。这可不好。

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:01.010
<v Chickenman>Anything else?
<v Chickenman>还有什么吗？

00:51:01.010 --> 00:51:02.850
<v Doctor>Yes, you are ugly.
<v Doctor>是的，你很丑。

00:51:02.850 --> 00:51:05.530
<v Chickenman>That's my chicken mask, the beak and the feathers.
<v Chickenman>那是我的鸡面具，鸟喙和羽毛。

00:51:05.530 --> 00:51:06.450
<v Doctor>Anybody ever tell you it's ugly?
<v Doctor>有人跟你说过它很丑吗？

00:51:06.450 --> 00:51:10.630
<v Chickenman>Well, that's the idea. Otherwise, I couldn't strike terror into the hearts of vicious criminals everywhere.
<v Chickenman>嗯，这正是目的所在。否则我就无法让各地恶贯满盈的罪犯闻风丧胆了。

00:51:10.630 --> 00:51:24.380
<v Doctor>Aha, well don't look at small children or animals. Anyway, that's the health story, but I don't think you have to alter your lifestyle unless you are a crime-fighting superhero of some kind. [LAUGHS] Want to buy one of my tapes?
<v Doctor>啊哈，好吧，别看着小孩或动物。总之，这就是健康方面的情况，但除非你是某种打击犯罪的超级英雄，否则我觉得你没必要改变生活方式。[笑]想买我的磁带吗？

00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:44.370
<v Chickenman>12:00 noon. I return to the chicken cave, and there in the chicken mirror-- ah!-- I see something horrible. No, not my ugly face, my own mortality. I ask myself why it never stared me in the face before. After all, I've been fighting crime and or evil for over 30 years, pursuing it down streets and alleys and sewers and other picturesque places, and my mortality never came up even once.
<v Chickenman>12:00 中午。我回到鸡窟，在那里，在鸡镜子里——啊！——我看到了可怕的东西。不，不是我那张丑脸，而是我自己的死亡。我问自己为什么以前从未直面过它。毕竟，我已经打击犯罪或邪恶30多年了，在街道、小巷、下水道和其他如画的地方追捕它们，而我的死亡甚至一次都没出现过。

00:51:44.370 --> 00:51:58.090
<v Chickenman>1:40 PM. I go see the police commissioner and share with him the doctor's diagnosis. After all, he is my closest friend, and if I can't tell him the bad news, who can I tell? So I give him a new coloring book I bought for him and tell him my sad news. And he says--
<v Chickenman>1:40 PM。我去见警察局长，与他分享医生的诊断结果。毕竟，他是我最好的朋友，如果我不能把坏消息告诉他，我还能告诉谁呢？所以我给了他一本我买给他的新涂色书，并告诉他我的坏消息。他说——

00:51:58.090 --> 00:52:01.440
<v Commissioner>Uh-huh. This looks like a real neat coloring book.
<v Commissioner>嗯哼。这看起来像是一本非常漂亮的涂色书。

00:52:01.440 --> 00:52:03.330
<v Chickenman>So what do you think, Commissioner?
<v Chickenman>所以你怎么看，局长？

00:52:03.330 --> 00:52:04.250
<v Commissioner>About what?
<v Commissioner>关于什么？

00:52:04.250 --> 00:52:05.260
<v Chickenman>What I just shared with you?
<v Chickenman>我刚才跟你分享的事情？

00:52:05.260 --> 00:52:07.870
<v Commissioner>Oh, it's a real neat coloring book.
<v Commissioner>噢，这是一本非常漂亮的涂色书。

00:52:07.870 --> 00:52:10.580
<v Chickenman>About the diagnosis and the need to alter my lifestyle.
<v Chickenman>关于诊断结果以及我需要改变生活方式的必要性。

00:52:10.580 --> 00:52:18.190
<v Commissioner>Oh, well that would mean that you'd have to-- and of course one cant even be sure that, you know-- so anyway that's how I see it.
<v Commissioner>噢，嗯，那意味着你将不得不——当然，没人能确定，你知道——所以，这就是我的看法。

00:52:18.190 --> 00:52:19.570
<v Chickenman>OK, thanks, Commissioner.
<v Chickenman>好的，谢谢你，局长。

00:52:19.570 --> 00:52:23.890
<v Commissioner>Anytime, winged warrior. After all, what are friends for? And may I ask you a question?
<v Commissioner>随时欢迎，长翅膀的战士。毕竟，朋友是干什么的呢？我可以问你一个问题吗？

00:52:23.890 --> 00:52:24.700
<v Chickenman>OK.
<v Chickenman>好的。

00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:29.000
<v Commissioner>If I make the sky blue in this picture and the mountains brown, do you think the rocks should be chartreuse?
<v Commissioner>如果我把这张画里的天空涂成蓝色，山涂成棕色，你觉得岩石应该涂成黄绿色吗？

00:52:29.000 --> 00:52:34.760
<v Chickenman>Perfect. 4:00 PM. I go to the local office of the Gracehill Fergus employment agency and screen door company.
<v Chickenman>完美。4:00 PM。我去当地的格雷斯希尔·弗格斯职业介绍所和纱门公司。

00:52:34.760 --> 00:52:39.350
<v Employment Agent>OK, when you say something more sed-rentary like what do you mean?
<v Employment Agent>好吧，当你提到“更沉静一点”的工作时，你是什么意思？

00:52:39.350 --> 00:52:42.530
<v Chickenman>No, sedentary you know, things where I can seden--sit.
<v Chickenman>不，是久坐不动（sedentary），你知道，可以让我坐着的工作。

00:52:42.530 --> 00:52:44.640
<v Employment Agent>Oh, OK, so something sit-entary.
<v Employment Agent>噢，好的，所以是“坐着”工作。

00:52:44.640 --> 00:52:45.090
<v Chickenman>Yeah.
<v Chickenman>是啊。

00:52:45.090 --> 00:52:51.660
<v Employment Agent>I just started here. I'm supposed to ask some questions. What kind of previous work experience do you have?
<v Employment Agent>我刚来这儿。我得问几个问题。你以前有什么工作经验？

00:52:51.660 --> 00:52:54.200
<v Chickenman>Basically fighting crime and or evil.
<v Chickenman>基本上是打击犯罪或邪恶。

00:52:54.200 --> 00:53:00.990
<v Employment Agent>OK, and what special equipment, office or otherwise, are you experienced in using?
<v Employment Agent>好的，你擅长使用什么特殊的办公设备或其他设备吗？

00:53:00.990 --> 00:53:01.800
<v Chickenman>Geshtukana ray gun.
<v Chickenman>格什图卡纳光线枪。

00:53:01.800 --> 00:53:02.980
<v Employment Agent>Could you spell that?
<v Employment Agent>你能拼写一下吗？

00:53:02.980 --> 00:53:08.280
<v Chickenman>G-E-S-H-T-U-K-N-A. And I also worked a chicken dissolver and a chicken modulator and a can opener.
<v Chickenman>G-E-S-H-T-U-K-N-A。我还操作过鸡溶解器、鸡调制器和开罐器。

00:53:08.280 --> 00:53:09.820
<v Employment Agent>T-U-K--
<v Employment Agent>T-U-K——

00:53:09.820 --> 00:53:12.880
<v Chickenman>A-N-A. So what do you have in light work that I could do?
<v Chickenman>A-N-A。那么你们有什么我可以做的轻松工作吗？

00:53:12.880 --> 00:53:14.560
<v Employment Agent>A-N--
<v Employment Agent>A-N——

00:53:14.560 --> 00:53:16.180
<v Chickenman>A. That's it. Geshtukana. You got it?
<v Chickenman>A。就是这个。格什图卡纳。记住了吗？

00:53:16.180 --> 00:53:19.260
<v Employment Agent>OK, do you know Windows 95?
<v Employment Agent>好的，你会用Windows 95吗？

00:53:19.260 --> 00:53:22.330
<v Chickenman>Look, what light job openings are on your list there? Just look.
<v Chickenman>听着，你们清单上有什么轻松的工作岗位吗？看看就行。

00:53:22.330 --> 00:53:27.170
<v Employment Agent>Heavy cable puller, refrigerator and piano mover, cement hailer--
<v Employment Agent>重型电缆牵引工、冰箱和钢琴搬运工、水泥拖运——

00:53:27.170 --> 00:53:28.100
<v Chickenman>Hauler.
<v Chickenman>拖运（Hauler）。

00:53:28.100 --> 00:53:31.270
<v Employment Agent>OK. [SCREAMING] Big tree planter, circus tent.
<v Employment Agent>好的。[尖叫]大树种植工、马戏团帐篷。

00:53:31.270 --> 00:53:35.600
<v Chickenman>Miss, not holler. Those are all active and heavy things. Anything light I could do?
<v Chickenman>小姐，不是搬运（Holler）。那些都是活跃且繁重的活。有什么我可以做的轻松工作吗？

00:53:35.600 --> 00:53:38.520
<v Employment Agent>Yes, a negligee model in a delicatessen.
<v Employment Agent>是的，熟食店的睡衣模特。

00:53:38.520 --> 00:53:39.240
<v Chickenman>I don't wear--
<v Chickenman>我不穿——

00:53:39.240 --> 00:53:44.780
<v Employment Agent>Oh, well, scratch that then. Requires previous experience. Oh, here's something really perfect.
<v Employment Agent>噢，好吧，那就算了。需要相关经验。噢，这儿有个完美的。

00:53:44.780 --> 00:53:45.520
<v Chickenman>What's that?
<v Chickenman>什么？

00:53:45.520 --> 00:53:53.960
<v Employment Agent>A napkin folder in a nouveau Italian-Chinese restaurant specializing in pizza and light salads. Takeout available. Mmm, I'm hungry.
<v Employment Agent>一家新派意大利-中国餐厅的餐巾折叠工，专门做比萨和清淡沙拉。可外带。唔，我饿了。

00:53:53.960 --> 00:54:05.690
<v Chickenman>Wednesday morning, 9:30 AM. My chicken alarm goes off a half hour late for my geriatric counseling appointment. Tire still flat. So I take the convenient number 18 bus, and that leaves me off only 28 blocks from the counselor's office.
<v Chickenman>周三早上，9:30。我的鸡报警器又晚了半小时响，耽误了我的老年咨询预约。轮胎还是瘪的。所以我坐了方便的18路公交车，它把我放在离咨询师办公室只有28个街区的地方。

00:54:05.690 --> 00:54:08.430
<v Counselor>I have one word of advice, mister. Get out.
<v Counselor>我有一句话要送给你，先生。出去。

00:54:08.430 --> 00:54:08.960
<v Chickenman>Excuse me?
<v Chickenman>对不起？

00:54:08.960 --> 00:54:09.410
<v Counselor>Get out.
<v Counselor>出去。

00:54:09.410 --> 00:54:10.810
<v Chickenman>Do you mean from this office?
<v Chickenman>你是说离开这个办公室吗？

00:54:10.810 --> 00:54:13.070
<v Counselor>I mean get out. O-U-T.
<v Counselor>我是说出去。O-U-T。

00:54:13.070 --> 00:54:14.660
<v Chickenman>OK, I'm a few minutes late.
<v Chickenman>好吧，我迟到了几分钟。

00:54:14.660 --> 00:54:16.870
<v Counselor>You're 30 years too late. Get out.
<v Counselor>你迟到了30年。出去。

00:54:16.870 --> 00:54:17.880
<v Chickenman>Oh, you mean get out, not get out.
<v Chickenman>噢，你是说离开，不是那种“出去”。

00:54:17.880 --> 00:54:23.910
<v Counselor>May I suggest a small desert superhero retirement community. You play golf?
<v Counselor>我可以建议一个小型的沙漠超级英雄退休社区吗？你打高尔夫球吗？

00:54:23.910 --> 00:54:25.260
<v Chickenman>Not real good, no.
<v Chickenman>打得不太好，没。

00:54:25.260 --> 00:54:30.390
<v Counselor>Good, you'll fit right in. Neither does Fishwoman or that flying newt. I sent them there. They love it.
<v Counselor>很好，你正合适。鱼女和那只飞蝾螈也不行。我把她们送去那儿了。她们很喜欢。

00:54:30.390 --> 00:54:31.250
<v Chickenman>Fishwoman?
<v Chickenman>鱼女？

00:54:31.250 --> 00:54:33.510
<v Counselor>Yeah, a little scaly, nice personality.
<v Counselor>是啊，身上有点鳞片，性格很好。

00:54:33.510 --> 00:54:34.400
<v Chickenman>OK.
<v Chickenman>好的。

00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:35.500
<v Counselor>Want to buy one of my tapes?
<v Counselor>想买我的磁带吗？

00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:50.290
<v Chickenman>2:00 AM next morning. I can't sleep, and I sip warm milk in the chicken cave. What to do? I'm on the horns of a dilemma. Heavy concrete hauler? Fold napkins in nouveau Italian-Chinese restaurant specializing in pizza and light salads? Or challenge the fates?
<v Chickenman>第二天凌晨2:00。我睡不着，在鸡窟里喝着温牛奶。该怎么办？我陷入了进退两难的境地。重型水泥拖运工？在新派意大利-中国餐厅折叠餐巾？还是挑战命运？

00:54:50.290 --> 00:55:09.240
<v Chickenman>8:00 AM. I stand on the roof of the Midland City's skyscraper, four dizzy stories high. I hurl a challenge to the fates. "This is the winged warrior, fates. I shall go on fighting crime and or evil. I don't care that my bad cholesterol is bad, that--" Suddenly, a black cloud forms swiftly in the sky, and I hear--
<v Chickenman>早上8:00。我站在米德兰市摩天大楼的楼顶，四层楼高。我向命运发出挑战。“我是长翅膀的战士，命运。我将继续打击犯罪或邪恶。我不在乎我的坏胆固醇很坏，不在乎——”突然，天空迅速形成一朵乌云，我听到——

00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:17.050
<v Frank>OK, do what you want. We'll try to be there for you, but watch the fatty foods, the cookies, the ice cream, and good luck to you.
<v Frank>好吧，你想做什么就做什么吧。我们会试着支持你，但注意那些高脂肪食物、饼干、冰淇淋，祝你好运。

00:55:17.050 --> 00:55:17.480
<v Chickenman>Who is that?
<v Chickenman>那是谁？

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:18.710
<v Frank>One of the fates.
<v Frank>其中一个命运。

00:55:18.710 --> 00:55:19.350
<v Chickenman>Which one?
<v Chickenman>哪一个？

00:55:19.350 --> 00:55:25.420
<v Frank>Frank. Phyllis, Fran, and Fred are in Las Vegas. God bless them. They should only win and be well.
<v Frank>弗兰克。菲利斯、弗兰和弗雷德在拉斯维加斯。上帝保佑她们。祝她们赢钱，身体健康。

00:55:25.420 --> 00:55:27.900
<v Chickenman>OK, well, fine, I'll just carry on then.
<v Chickenman>好的，好吧，那我继续吧。

00:55:27.900 --> 00:55:34.790
<v Frank>OK, listen, could you change that mask you're wearing? Now it's very ugly and could scare kids and small animals. Thank you very much.
<v Frank>好的，听着，你能换掉你戴的面具吗？现在它非常丑，可能会吓到小孩和动物。非常感谢。

00:55:34.790 --> 00:55:47.760
<v Chickenman>Right. And at that moment, I knew fate was blind, and I, the famous fowl, would have the last laugh. For you see, I wasn't wearing a mask. [LAUGHS]
<v Chickenman>好吧。那一刻，我知道命运是盲目的，而我，著名的禽类，将笑到最后。因为你看，我根本没戴面具。[笑]

00:55:47.760 --> 00:56:19.840
<v Chickenman Announcer>Well, what has the winged warrior gotten himself into here? Can he actually stop time by challenging the fates? And is it Frank Fate he's talking to or George Jessel? And another thing, doesn't that nouveau Italian-Chinese restaurant sound super trendy? Be listening tomorrow for another exciting episode in the life of the most fantastic crime fighter the world has ever known, Chickenman.
<v Chickenman Announcer>好了，长翅膀的战士把自己卷入了什么事里？他真的能通过挑战命运来停止时间吗？他是在跟弗兰克·命运说话，还是跟乔治·杰塞尔？还有，那家新派意大利-中国餐厅听起来不觉得超级时髦吗？明天继续收听世界上最了不起的犯罪克星——鸡侠生命中又一段激动人心的插曲。

00:56:19.840 --> 00:56:23.200
<v Women>He's everywhere! He's everywhere!
<v Women>他无处不在！他无处不在！

00:56:23.200 --> 00:57:42.880
<v Ira Glass>Well, "Chickenman Challenges a Fate Named Frank" was recorded at Dick Orkin's radio ranch in Hollywood, California. Along with Dick Orkin, the cast included Allison Ann Martin, Miriam Flynn, Charlie Brill, and Jim Gallant. Engineers Elizabeth Lane and James [? Burns, ?] written by Dick Orkin and Christine Coyle. Miss Flynn's hairstyle by Mr. Bunny. If you want more information about Chickenman , it is on the internet with sound files that you can get at this address, www.radio-ranch.com.
<v Ira Glass>“鸡侠挑战命运弗兰克”是在加州好莱坞迪克·奥金的广播牧场录制的。除了迪克·奥金，演员还包括艾莉森·安·马丁、米里亚姆·弗林、查理·布里尔和吉姆·加兰特。工程师伊丽莎白·莱恩和詹姆斯·伯恩斯，剧本由迪克·奥金和克里斯汀·科伊尔创作。弗林小姐的发型由邦尼先生设计。如果你想了解更多关于鸡侠的信息，可以在互联网上获取音频文件，地址是 www.radio-ranch.com。

00:57:42.880 --> 00:57:51.100
<v Ira Glass>Well, today's program was produced by Nancy Updike, Peter Clowney, Alix Spiegel, Dolores Wilber, and myself. Contributing editors Margy Rochlin, Paul Tough, and Jack Hitt.
<v Ira Glass>好了，今天的节目由南希·厄普代克、彼得·克劳尼、阿利克斯·斯皮格尔、多洛雷斯·威尔伯和我制作。特约编辑马吉·罗克林、保罗·塔夫和杰克·希特。

00:57:51.100 --> 00:58:01.540
<v Ira Glass>[ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS]
<v Ira Glass>[鸣谢]

00:58:01.540 --> 00:58:08.980
<v Danielle>I just want a real person who's like Duki probably. I want to go marry some guy who's like Duki.
<v Danielle>我只是想要一个真正像杜基那样的人。我想嫁给一个像杜基一样的家伙。

00:58:08.980 --> 00:58:10.920
<v Ira Glass>And how is that search going?
<v Ira Glass>那寻找进展如何？

00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:11.870
<v Danielle>Not well.
<v Danielle>不怎么样。

00:58:11.870 --> 00:58:30.020
<v Ira Glass>If you'd like to buy a copy of this or any of our This American Life programs, they make a fine stocking stuffer. Christmas is coming up. Don't delay. Call us at WBEZ here in Chicago, 312-832-3380. 312-832-3380. The cost is $10.
<v Ira Glass>如果你想买本节目或我们任何一期《美国生活》的副本，它们是很好的长筒袜填充礼物。圣诞节快到了。别耽误。请致电我们芝加哥的WBEZ电台，电话312-832-3380。312-832-3380。费用是10美元。

00:58:30.020 --> 00:58:39.320
<v Ira Glass>[FUNDING CREDITS]
<v Ira Glass>[资金鸣谢]

00:58:39.320 --> 00:58:43.380
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ management oversight by Torey Malatia. I'm Ira Glass.
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ管理监督由托里·马拉蒂亚负责。我是艾拉·格拉斯。

00:58:43.380 --> 00:58:47.590
<v Danielle>Ira, don't make me sound like an idiot, OK?
<v Danielle>艾拉，别把我弄得像个白痴，好吗？

00:58:47.590 --> 00:58:49.040
<v Ira Glass>Done.
<v Ira Glass>搞定。

00:58:49.040 --> 00:58:54.040
<v Ira Glass>Back next week with more stories of This American Life .
<v Ira Glass>下周回来收听更多《美国生活》的故事。
